# Cursor AI Development Rules for SQL PT Project

## 🎯 Project Context
This is a Next.js 14 TypeScript project with React, Tailwind CSS, and Radix UI components.

## 📋 Mandatory Rules

### 1. UI/UX Patterns (MANDATORY)
**ALWAYS follow the patterns defined in `frontend/docs/UI_UX_PATTERNS.md`**

- ✅ Use `<form>` with `onSubmit` for all forms (Enter key support)
- ✅ Use `ConfirmationDialog` for delete confirmations (NEVER use `confirm()`)
- ✅ Use `PageLoader` for page-level loading states
- ✅ Use `Loader2` with `animate-spin` for button-level loading
- ✅ Implement field-level validation with error states
- ✅ Clear validation errors when user types
- ✅ Add `aria-label` and `title` to all icon-only buttons
- ✅ Use `Label` component with `htmlFor` for form labels

### 2. Component Structure (MANDATORY)
**Follow the structure in `frontend/docs/COMPONENT_ARCHITECTURE.md`**

```typescript
// 1. Imports (grouped)
// 2. Type definitions
// 3. Constants
// 4. Main component
// 5. Helper functions
```

### 3. File Naming
- Components: `kebab-case.tsx`
- Pages: `page.tsx` (Next.js convention)
- Utilities: `kebab-case.ts`
- Hooks: `use-kebab-case.ts`

### 4. Code Organization
- State: Group by purpose (loading, data, UI, errors)
- Handlers: Group by action type (submit, delete, edit, UI)
- Effects: At top after state declarations

### 5. Error Handling
- Always use toast notifications for errors
- User-friendly error messages
- Field-level errors for validation
- Never show raw error objects to users

### 6. Loading States
- Page-level: `<PageLoader message="..." />`
- Button-level: `<Loader2 className="h-4 w-4 animate-spin" />`
- Always show loading message
- Disable buttons during loading

### 7. Form Validation
- Validation errors in state: `const [formErrors, setFormErrors] = useState<FormErrors>({})`
- Validate function: `const validateForm = (): FormErrors => { ... }`
- Show errors under fields: `{formErrors.field && <p className="text-sm text-destructive">...</p>}`
- Highlight invalid fields: `className={formErrors.field ? "border-destructive" : ""}`
- Clear errors on change

### 8. Dialogs
- Reset state on close
- Clear errors on close
- Use `ConfirmationDialog` for destructive actions
- Escape key support (automatic with Radix UI)

### 9. Accessibility
- Icon-only buttons: `aria-label` + `title` REQUIRED
- Form labels: `Label` with `htmlFor` REQUIRED
- Loading states: `aria-label` or text REQUIRED
- Error messages: `role="alert"` for important errors

### 10. Keyboard Navigation
- Enter key: Works with `<form onSubmit>`
- Escape key: Works with Radix UI Dialog
- Tab order: Logical and predictable

## 🚫 NEVER Do

- ❌ NEVER use `confirm()` - Use `ConfirmationDialog`
- ❌ NEVER use `console.log` in production code
- ❌ NEVER skip validation
- ❌ NEVER skip error handling
- ❌ NEVER skip loading states
- ❌ NEVER skip accessibility attributes
- ❌ NEVER use inline styles (use Tailwind)
- ❌ NEVER create custom components that duplicate UI library functionality

## ✅ ALWAYS Do

- ✅ Read `UI_UX_PATTERNS.md` before starting any feature
- ✅ Follow component structure template
- ✅ Use TypeScript interfaces for all props
- ✅ Use design system constants from `@/lib/design-system`
- ✅ Use existing UI components from `@/components/ui`
- ✅ Test keyboard navigation
- ✅ Test with screen readers (accessibility)
- ✅ Handle all error cases
- ✅ Show loading states
- ✅ Provide user feedback (toasts)

## 📚 Required Reading Before Development

1. `frontend/docs/UI_UX_PATTERNS.md` - Development patterns
2. `frontend/docs/COMPONENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` - File structure
3. `frontend/lib/design-system.ts` - Design constants

## 🔍 Code Review Checklist

Before submitting code, verify:
- [ ] Follows UI/UX patterns
- [ ] Follows component structure
- [ ] All forms have validation
- [ ] All errors are handled
- [ ] Loading states implemented
- [ ] Accessibility attributes present
- [ ] Keyboard navigation works
- [ ] No `console.log` statements
- [ ] TypeScript types defined
- [ ] Error messages are user-friendly

## 🎨 Design System

Use constants from `@/lib/design-system`:
- Spacing: `spacing[4]` for consistent spacing
- Typography: `typography.sm` for font sizes
- Colors: `colors.status.error` for error states
- Layout: `layout.container.lg` for container widths

## 🔗 Component Imports

Always import from correct paths:
- UI Components: `@/components/ui/[component]`
- Custom Components: `@/components/[feature]/[component]`
- Utilities: `@/lib/[utility]`
- Types: Define in same file or `@/types/[type]`

## 💡 Development Workflow

1. Read relevant documentation
2. Check existing similar components
3. Follow patterns exactly
4. Test all interactions
5. Verify accessibility
6. Check keyboard navigation
7. Review error handling
8. Verify loading states

## 🎯 AI Development Instructions

When developing new features:
1. **First**: Read `UI_UX_PATTERNS.md` completely
2. **Second**: Check existing similar components for reference
3. **Third**: Follow patterns exactly - do not customize or deviate
4. **Fourth**: Use existing UI components - do not create new ones
5. **Fifth**: Test all requirements from checklist

**Remember**: Consistency is more important than creativity. Follow the established patterns.



